{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Then the land shall be appeased</b> — this word is like תשלי׳‎, and likewise עד ירצה כשכיר יומו, for her iniquity is appeased." "<b>Its sabbaths.</b> The sabbatical years and jubilees, and so it is written עד רצתה הארץ את שבתותיה, and there I explained it." "<b>Desolation.</b> There [=שמה], and the patterns of the nouns vary." "And the meaning of <b>all the days of its desolation while you are in the land of your enemies</b> — that it will be desolate of you; then it shall rest and find repose to fulfill its sabbaths."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:49.733435625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}